    "q-96279": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96279",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ compute $P(W\\le 5).$",
      "worked_solution": "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\le 5) & =P(3\\le W\\le 5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{5-3}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
